  "question": {
    "text": "A bird is sitting on the top of a vertical pole <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> high and its elevation from a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> on the ground is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It flies off horizontally straight away from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>. After one second, the elevation of the bird from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is reduced to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Then the speed (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>) of the bird is&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
